<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>FAQs - Turtle Shelter Project</title>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0-alpha3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="css/bootstrap-icons.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="css/templatemo-kind-heart-charity.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/custom.css">
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Header -->
    <%- include('partials/header') %>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main class="container my-5">
        <h1 class="mb-4 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
        <div class="accordion" id="faqAccordion">
            
            <!-- FAQ Item 1 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading1">
                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapse1">
                        How long have you been doing this?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" aria-labelledby="heading1" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        Jen conceived the Turtle Shelter Project in 2015 to prevent individuals experiencing homelessness from succumbing to freezing temperatures. The organization was officially incorporated on April 3, 2017, coinciding with Jen's sobriety anniversary, and attained 501(c)(3) status in 2018. Between September 2017 and January 2018, with a combined 450 volunteer hours, 50 prototype vests were completed for testing.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 2 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading2">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse2">
                        If you want to help homeless people be warm, why not just do a coat drive?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading2" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        The vests utilize a foam insulation layer combined with moisture-wicking fabrics, creating a more effective insulation than standard winter clothing. This design maintains warmth even when wet, allowing wearers to preserve their core body temperature. More details are available in the "Our Tech" section.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 3 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading3">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse3">
                        What does the turtle in your logo have to do with your project?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading3" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        A turtle carries its shelter wherever it goes. Similarly, the insulated vests are intended to serve as portable "shelters," enabling individuals to carry their shelter on their back, akin to a turtle.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 4 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading4">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse4">
                        How/where are the vests distributed?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading4" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        During the winter of 2017-18, distribution and testing occurred mainly in the Ogden area, with support from The Episcopal Church of the Good Shepherd and Youth Futures staff. In the winter of 2018-19, vests were distributed to shelters and individuals in the Ogden and Salt Lake City communities. A detailed list of donations can be found <a href="https://turtleshelterproject.org/vests-distributed">here</a>.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 5 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading5">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse5">
                        Why don’t you just have a professional sewing shop make the vests?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading5" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        The mission encompasses two parts: assisting those in need of warm clothing and providing opportunities for anyone willing to serve. This philosophy led to the motto: "Every Life Has Value; Every Person Can Serve."
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 6 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading6">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse6">
                        I want to help, but I don’t sew.
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading6" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        The vests are designed to be made by volunteers without specialized sewing skills. Tasks such as using a marker or scissors can be performed by anyone. While individuals with basic and advanced sewing skills are needed, many steps can be completed by those without sewing experience. Final construction is handled by expert staff, and completed vests are returned to the community where they were made or sent to other areas in need.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 7 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading7">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse7">
                        We don’t live close to your Northern Utah operation. Can we still help?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading7" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        Absolutely! Materials can be sent to your group for cutting, marking, or completion, which can then be returned or distributed in your area. The organization believes that every person can serve and will accommodate anyone willing to help, limited only by funding. Contact them through the <a href="https://turtleshelterproject.org/contact-us">Contact Us</a> or <a href="https://turtleshelterproject.org/schedule-your-own-event">Schedule Your Own Event</a> pages to coordinate a suitable project.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 8 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading8">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse8">
                        How much of my donation goes to overhead?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading8" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        The organization strives to minimize overhead costs, ensuring that the majority of donations directly support the mission. Specific financial details can be provided upon request.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Item 9 -->
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading9">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse9" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse9">
                        How can I get involved?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse9" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading9" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        There are various ways to participate, including volunteering time, donating materials or funds, organizing events, or spreading awareness. Visit the <a href="https://turtleshelterproject.org/get-involved">Get Involved</a> page for more information.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </main>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <%- include('partials/footer') %>

    <!-- JavaScript Files -->
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0-alpha3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
    <script src="js/custom.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

